  "reviews": [
    {
      "author": "Simon Foster",
      "content": "\"With scribe Stephen Susco and a committed ensemble leaning into the full potential of the sci-fi premise, [director Steven] Quale delivers a surprise-upon-surprise romp that Rod Serling himself might have once conjured...\"\r\n**READ the full review here**: _http://www.screen-space.net/reviews/2026/6/16/black-box.html_",
      "rating": null,
      "createdAt": "2026-06-16T01:40:51Z"
    },
    {
      "author": "Sierbahnn",
      "content": "There's a lot of The Mist in here, and there's also a lot of Twilight Zone in here. Then there is some Invasion of the Body Snatchers, some Snakes on a plane. There's simply a lot here. Not all of it is bad, and it's an enjoyable ride, even though it has its flaws.",
      "rating": 6,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-16T17:41:42Z"
    },
    {
      "author": "the_original_crt",
      "content": "A unique alien body snatcher airline hi-jacking scifi thriller. Enjoyed the movie with its unexpected twists and turns. The premise might be a bit over the top but it is creative nonetheless. 7/10",
      "rating": 7,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-24T19:28:21Z"
    }
  ],
